      "title": "IDs and Clocks: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "IDs and Clocks: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Distributed ID Needs",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Unique== across every node: the one hard rule",
                "{green:k-sortable}: roughly time-ordered",
                "{green:Compact}: fewer bytes in every index",
                "{green:No coordination}: any node mints IDs alone"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Kinds of Clock",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Physical",
                "Logical"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Answers",
                  "==when== did it happen",
                  "==what happened before what=="
                ],
                [
                  "Hardware",
                  "needs synced clocks",
                  "{green:never} needs synced hardware"
                ],
                [
                  "Form",
                  "timestamp",
                  "counter"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Happens-Before",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`a → b` if same process and ==a is earlier==",
                "`a → b` if a is a ==send== and b its ==receive==",
                "No path either way: {orange:concurrent}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Key Order and the B-tree",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Key",
                "Insert lands",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Time-ordered",
                  "right edge",
                  "{green:fast, cache-friendly}"
                ],
                [
                  "Random",
                  "anywhere",
                  "{red:page splits, cache misses}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Timestamps say ==when==; only happens-before says **what caused what**. Concurrent events have no true order."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ID Schemes: Auto-increment, UUIDs, Snowflake, Ticket Servers",
      "role": "outline",
