      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ID Schemes: Auto-increment, UUIDs, Snowflake, Ticket Servers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Auto-increment and UUIDs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Auto-increment: ==8-byte==, sorted, tiny index",
                "{red:Single writer} is a bottleneck; it ==leaks row counts==",
                "Multi-master needs ==offset/step==: node 1 gives 1,3,5; node 2 gives 2,4,6"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Scheme",
                "Size / bits",
                "Sorted?",
                "Coordination"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Auto-increment",
                  "8 bytes",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "single writer"
                ],
                [
                  "UUID v4",
                  "16 bytes, 122 random bits",
                  "{red:no}, fragments clustered index",
                  "{green:none}, collisions negligible"
                ],
                [
                  "UUID v7",
                  "48-bit Unix-ms prefix + random",
                  "{green:yes}",
                  "{green:none}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Snowflake (64 bits)",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "1 bit",
                    "sub": "sign",
                    "ink": "black"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "41 bits",
                    "sub": "ms timestamp, ~69 years from custom epoch",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "10 bits",
                    "sub": "worker ID",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "12 bits",
                    "sub": "sequence, 4096 IDs per ms per worker",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Timestamp comes first, so IDs ==sort by time==",
                "Each worker needs a ==unique worker ID=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Ticket Server (Flickr)",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "REPLACE INTO Tickets64 (stub) VALUES ('a');",
                "SELECT LAST_INSERT_ID();"
              ],
              "note": "a dedicated DB hands out the next ID"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Run ==two servers== with odd/even steps",
                "Clients ==cache a block== of IDs: no round trip per ID"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "v4 is unsorted. Auto-increment needs one writer. ==v7== is sorted and coordination-free."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clock Skew, NTP and Why Wall Clocks Lie",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Clock Skew, NTP and Why Wall Clocks Lie",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Skew vs Drift",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Skew== = offset between two nodes' clocks",
                "==Drift== = rate a clock gains or loses time",
                "Quartz drifts roughly {blue:tens of ppm}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. NTP and Monotonic Clocks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "NTP accuracy: ==~ms== on a LAN, ==tens of ms== over the internet",
                "NTP can **step the clock backward**: wall time is not monotonic"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Clock",
                "Use for",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Monotonic**",
                  "durations, timeouts",
                  "`CLOCK_MONOTONIC`, `System.nanoTime`"
                ],
                [
                  "**Wall**",
                  "timestamps only",
                  "`System.currentTimeMillis`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. What Breaks",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Last-write-wins on wall clocks silently drops writes",
                "The node with the ==fast clock== always wins",
                "Snowflake and UUIDv7 break on a backward jump"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Clock goes back",
                    "sub": "now < last_timestamp",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Refuse",
                    "sub": "issue no IDs",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Wait it out",
                    "sub": "until caught up",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bump sequence",
                    "sub": "keep last_timestamp",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Never compare raw wall clocks across nodes to order events. Use ==monotonic== for elapsed time."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Logical Clocks: Lamport, Vector, Hybrid",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Logical Clocks: Lamport, Vector, Hybrid",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lamport Clock",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Local event",
                    "note": "c = c + 1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Send",
                    "note": "attach c",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Receive",
                    "note": "c = max(local, received) + 1",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "a → b implies ==L(a) < L(b)==",
                "Converse is {red:false}: L(a) < L(b) proves nothing",
                "Equal or ordered stamps cannot show causality or concurrency"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Vector Clock",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One counter per node==, compared element-wise",
                "Neither vector dominates → events are ==concurrent== (a conflict)",
                "Cost grows with the **number of nodes**",
                "Dynamo-style stores keep **sibling versions**, then merge or let the client resolve"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Vectors",
                "Verdict"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "[1,2,0] vs [2,2,0]",
                  "first {green:happened before} second"
                ],
                [
                  "[2,0,0] vs [1,1,0]",
                  "{red:concurrent}: resolve"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Hybrid Logical Clock",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "HLC = (physical time ==l==, logical counter ==c==)",
                "Stays close to wall time, yet **causal**",
                "Used by CockroachDB and MongoDB",
                "Bounded ==max-offset== check rejects clocks too far ahead"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Lamport gives order, not concurrency. Only ==vector clocks== detect concurrent events."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ordering Guarantees in Partitioned Systems",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Ordering Guarantees in Partitioned Systems",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Order Per Partition",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Kafka orders only ==within a partition==",
                "Partition key (`user_id`) keeps related events together",
                "No order guarantee across partitions"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Producer",
                    "sub": "key = user_id",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Partition",
                    "sub": "one per key",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Consumer",
                    "sub": "dedupe on event ID",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Total order needs ==one partition==, a **sequencer**, or **consensus** (Raft/Paxos)",
                "Cost: lower throughput, higher latency",
                "Common design: per-key order + ==idempotent consumers==",
                "Dedupe on `event ID` or sequence number"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Retries Can Reorder",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Idempotence",
                "In-flight per connection",
                "Order"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{green:on}",
                  "up to 5",
                  "{green:kept}"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:off}",
                  "1",
                  "{green:kept}"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:off}",
                  "more than 1",
                  "{red:reordered}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Spanner TrueTime",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Returns a bounded interval [`earliest`, `latest`]",
                "==Commit-wait==: wait out the uncertainty before commit",
                "Result: **external consistency**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Order holds ==per key==. Global order costs throughput and latency."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Choosing IDs and Clocks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Choosing IDs and Clocks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Choosing an ID",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Single DB, internal-only IDs",
                  "==Auto-increment== (or bigint identity)"
                ],
                [
                  "Public or distributed, no sorting needed",
                  "==UUID v4=="
                ],
                [
                  "DB primary key at scale",
                  "==UUID v7== or ==Snowflake=="
                ],
                [
                  "64-bit, compact, sortable",
                  "==Snowflake=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Snowflake worker ID: assign via ==ZooKeeper==, ==etcd== or config",
                "Sorting by ID gives only ==approximate== time order across workers (ms-level skew)",
                "Sequential IDs as public identifiers without authorization checks: ==enumeration risk=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing a Clock",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Causal order only",
                  "==Lamport=="
                ],
                [
                  "Detect concurrency",
                  "==Vector clock=="
                ],
                [
                  "Wall-time-like causal timestamps",
                  "==HLC=="
                ],
                [
                  "Durations and timeouts",
                  "==Monotonic clock=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cross-node ordering by raw wall-clock comparison",
                "Using the wall clock to measure a duration"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Rule of thumb",
              "text": "Wall clock for **timestamps**, monotonic clock for **durations**, logical clocks for **order**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
